    <TD STYLE="text-align: justify; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; vertical-align: top"><P STYLE="text-align: justify; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>from</B>
                                            US$1,000,000 divided into: (i) 1,500,000 Class A Ordinary Shares of a par value of US$0.6
                                            each; and (ii) 100,000,000 Class B ordinary shares of a par value of US$0.001 each to either,
                                            depending on the final ratio of the Share Consolidation <B>to</B> US$540,100,000 divided
                                            into 900,000,000 Class A Ordinary Shares, of a par value of US$0.6 each and (ii) 100,000,000
                                            Class B ordinary shares, of a par value of US$0.001 each <B>by</B> the creation of 898,500,000
                                            Class A Ordinary Shares, of par value US$0.6 each (the &#8220;Share Capital Increase&#8221;)</FONT></P></TD></TR>
